  - certified optimization
  - global optimization
  - Langevin dynamics
  - Hamiltonian Monte Carlo
abstract: >-
  NeuralOpt is a JAX research package in which a compact transformer proposes
  the update steps of a bounded numerical optimizer, with every objective and
  gradient evaluation counted against a shared budget. An opt-in compiled loop
  runs the learned rule as a single XLA program. A separate certified mode,
  which uses no learned component, proves bounds by interval branch-and-bound
  with outward rounding for a restricted expression subset, and its
  certificates can be replayed independently. The package is alpha research
  software. In the studies from v0.4 to v0.7 (pre-registered for v0.6
  and v0.7), the learned geometries did not beat validation-tuned fixed-diagonal or
  Barzilai-Borwein baselines, and classical L-BFGS outperforms the learned
  optimizer on the reported benchmarks.
